Looking at the zigzag cut edges: piece 1's left edge follows the sequence (down‑left, right, down‑right, long‑left, down‑right, down‑left), which is exactly the same as piece 3's right edge. Piece 1 supplies the right half of the hexagon (top side 30, two right slants, full bottom side), while piece 3 supplies the left half (top side 30, two left slants, left vertex, pointed bottom). Together their outer edges give the full hexagon: top 60, bottom 60, four slants of 60, left and right vertices.

Checking the other pairs: piece 2's cut edge (with the extra tab at the lower left) does not match piece 4's cut edge, and pieces 1 & 4 or 2 & 3 have mismatched notches or duplicate vertices, so they cannot close into a hexagon.

\boxed{B}
